# Use `fx.Int32(fx.lane_id)` for the lane index (Iluvatar backend)

**In Iluvatar kernel code, always compute the lane index from the hardware
intrinsic `fx.lane_id`, not from `tid % WARP_SIZE`.**

This rule targets the **Iluvatar backend** on this branch. Upstream AMD/CDNA/RDNA
kernels use their own idioms — they typically don't materialise a `lane_id`
variable via `tid % WARP_SIZE` at all (grep across `kernels/` confirms this
pattern only appears under `kernels/**/iluvatar/**`) — and are out of scope; do
not drive-by rewrite them.

```python
# ✅ GOOD — hardware intrinsic, single register read
lane_id = fx.Int32(fx.lane_id)

# ❌ BAD — synthesises the same value with a modulo the backend now has to
# recognise and optimise away
lane_id = tid % WARP_SIZE
```

## Why

- `fx.lane_id` (`python/flydsl/expr/gpu.py`: `lane_id = _ScalarGPUIndex(gpu.lane_id)`)
  lowers to a single hardware register read on Iluvatar via the FlyToIXDL
  conversion pipeline (`lib/Conversion/FlyToIXDL/`).
- `tid % WARP_SIZE` needs constant folding + strength reduction to become the
  same thing; the Iluvatar lowering pipeline does not always recognise the
  pattern and can emit a real modulo.
- The intrinsic form makes intent explicit: this value is the **lane
  identity**, not an arbitrary arithmetic result.

## Explicit `fx.Int32(...)` wrapping is required

`fx.lane_id` is a lazy `_ScalarGPUIndex` token; wrap it in `fx.Int32(...)` so it
materialises immediately and the resulting SSA value has an explicit type.
This mirrors the existing precedent in `kernels/gemm/iluvatar/mr/*.py`
(`hgemm.py`, `hgemm_splitk.py`, `small_m_hgemm.py`), which all use
`lane_id = fx.Int32(fx.lane_id)`. The stray `lane_id = tid % WARP_SIZE` in
`kernels/gemm/iluvatar/mr/igemm.py` L222 is exactly what this rule is meant to
prevent from spreading.

## Scope

- **Iluvatar backend only.** Upstream AMD/CDNA/RDNA kernels (`kernels/gemm/rdna_*`,
  `kernels/gemm/preshuffle_gemm.py`, `kernels/attention/flash_attn_*.py`,
  `kernels/moe/moe_gemm_2stage*`, gfx1250 files, etc.) are out of scope; do not
  migrate them.
- Applies to the lane index only. There is no analogous hardware intrinsic for
  `warp_id` (Iluvatar) / `wave_id` (legacy AMD/RDNA): keep computing those as
  `tid // WARP_SIZE` (Iluvatar) or `tid // WAVE_SIZE` (legacy AMD/RDNA, see
  `kernel-id-naming.mdc`).
- Applies inside `@flyc.kernel` / `@flyc.jit` bodies (kernel authoring). Test
  and host code are unaffected.

## Migration

- **New Iluvatar code**: MUST use `fx.Int32(fx.lane_id)` from the first line.
- **Iluvatar files being substantively edited** for another reason: fold the
  rename in.
- **Pure drive-by rewrite** in unrelated Iluvatar files: do **not** touch —
  only migrate when the user asks or the file is being edited anyway.
- **Non-Iluvatar files**: never migrate through this rule.
